# CQ 01: Which controls exist, and of which kind is each?
#
# 351-43-22 defines automating as implementing self-acting functions. The kind
# of control is the manner in which a control runs, which is why the
# control types are subclasses of control rather than a separate attribute.
#
# The most specific asserted type is reported, not every inferred superclass.
# Reporting the whole chain up to Control would only repeat what the class
# hierarchy already states.
#
# The pattern class is reached over the subclass hierarchy rather than by
# asking for it as a type. The reasoner materialises the direct type of an
# individual, so a query anchored on the general class alone returns nothing.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?control ?kind
WHERE {
  ?control a ?kind .
  ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Control .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?control a ?narrower .
    ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind .
    ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Control .
  }
} ORDER BY ?control ?kind
